# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# frontend environment
# Local: copy to frontend/.env.local  ·  Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here is needed on Vercel or locally: next.config.ts takes each deployment's URLs and cookie prefix from
# packages/shared/src/deployments.ts (Vercel's VERCEL_ENV picks production or staging; anywhere else is local).
# Set one only to override it, e.g. to test on a phone. Leave them out of Vercel's settings.

# ── API ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of the Express API for server-side calls (session checks, health). Docker sets http://backend:4000.
# API_URL=
# The API's address as the browser sees it (baked in at build time). Testing on a phone: http://<your LAN IP>:4000.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# ── Site ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical public URL (metadata, Open Graph, absolute links).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ── Auth ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session cookie name prefix; must match the API's AUTH_COOKIE_PREFIX.
# AUTH_COOKIE_PREFIX=
